# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Captured baseline evidence keeps every gate's raw output, including the coverage gate.
# The coverage.* rule above targets Go coverage profiles, not gate logs, and without this
# negation a baseline would silently commit six of its seven gates.
!**/baseline.logs/coverage.log
!**/baseline.logs/coverage.code

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep
frontend/package.json.md5
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/

# Feature 003 parity runs retain full per-case evidence locally, but the generated
# family/repetition image and raw-artifact tree is not source-controlled. Keep the
# compact top-level reports available for review and commit when appropriate.
/specs/003-real-files-and-tabs/evidence/ft-vs-08/parity/*/*

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store

build/bin/*

# Python bytecode from the specification checkers in scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
